  <h2>Average Salary by Age Group</h2>
  <p>
    Earnings in Canada follow a typical age-earnings profile: they rise steeply from ages 25 to 44 as
    workers gain experience and qualifications, plateau between ages 45 and 54, and then decline slightly
    approaching retirement age. Workers aged 25 to 34 earn significantly more than those 15 to 24, reflecting
    the transition from entry-level positions to established careers.
  </p>
