    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    <em>Source: Statistics Canada, Canadian Income Survey. Age groups represent all workers including part-time.</em>
  </p>

  <h2>Average Salary by Gender</h2>
  <p>
    The gender wage gap in Canada has narrowed over time but remains significant. As of 2025, women working
    full-time earn approximately 87 cents for every dollar earned by men in comparable roles. The gap varies
    by industry, occupation, and province. Factors contributing to the gap include occupational segregation,
    differences in hours worked, career interruptions, and underrepresentation in higher-paying industries
    such as mining, technology, and finance.
  </p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table>
      <thead>
